{"data":[{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2113382874422386688"]},"author_id":"215895007","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:31:57.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113382877358399739"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":9,"id":"5889072","start":0,"username":"wccftech"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/wccftech/statu…","end":278,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/wccftech/status/2113376629011669038","start":255,"url":"https://t.co/7pJtcJXcnd"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/x8gwKk6joY","end":302,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/juzzzzzzzzzzy/status/2113382877358399739/photo/1","media_key":"3_2113382874422386688","start":279,"url":"https://t.co/x8gwKk6joY"}]},"id":"2113382877358399739","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":4,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"@wccftech Your next laptop is stuck in line behind a datacenter. Every wafer that becomes HBM for an AI cluster eats ~3x the silicon a PC stick would've used. Memory isn't expensive because PCs are hot, it's expensive because hyperscalers ate the supply. https://t.co/7pJtcJXcnd https://t.co/x8gwKk6joY","url":"https://x.com/juzzzzzzzzzzy/status/2113382877358399739"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2113375390265696256"]},"author_id":"1010938256144420864","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:02:12.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113375392035639592"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/JMTpIShLNp","end":301,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/TechThought_org/status/2113375392035639592/photo/1","media_key":"3_2113375390265696256","start":278,"url":"https://t.co/JMTpIShLNp"}]},"id":"2113375392035639592","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":3,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Researchers engineered perforated silicon modulators using slow light 💡 to boost optical signal conversion efficiency across datacenter networks.   \n\nReplacing power-hungry copper connections with ultra-compact optical links 🔌 drastically cuts thermal load and cluster latency. https://t.co/JMTpIShLNp","url":"https://x.com/TechThought_org/status/2113375392035639592"},{"author_id":"1551376741402349568","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:59:30.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113374711430238355"],"entities":{"cashtags":[{"end":207,"start":203,"tag":"ATH"}],"hashtags":[{"end":212,"start":208,"tag":"ATH"},{"end":230,"start":213,"tag":"AIInfrastructure"},{"end":235,"start":231,"tag":"GPU"},{"end":251,"start":246,"tag":"B300"},{"end":255,"start":252,"tag":"AI"}],"mentions":[{"end":30,"id":"1531588175000268800","start":18,"username":"AethirCloud"},{"end":47,"id":"1983895448181207042","start":36,"username":"AxeCompute"},{"end":118,"id":"61559439","start":111,"username":"nvidia"},{"end":245,"id":"24920830","start":236,"username":"duostech"}],"urls":[{"description":"Discover how Axe Compute gained full ownership of its Georgia AI cluster, which is contracted through 2031 and expected to bring $364.6M in revenue.","display_url":"aethir.com/blog-posts/axe…","end":279,"expanded_url":"https://aethir.com/blog-posts/axe-compute-takes-full-ownership-of-georgia-ai-cluster-364-6m-expected-revenue","images":[{"height":632,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113374729335664640/cgGCuHgF?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1133},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113374729335664640/cgGCuHgF?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":256,"status":200,"title":"Axe Compute Takes Full Ownership of Georgia AI Cluster: $364.6M Expected Revenue | Aethir","unwound_url":"https://aethir.com/blog-posts/axe-compute-takes-full-ownership-of-georgia-ai-cluster-364-6m-expected-revenue","url":"https://t.co/6cAglwEjkT"}]},"id":"2113374711430238355","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":47,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"1/2🧵👇🏻\n🏗️ Oct. 6: @AethirCloud says @AxeCompute took 100% ownership of its Columbus, Georgia AI cluster: 2,304 @nvidia B300 GPUs, a customer contract extended through 2031 and ~$364.6M expected revenue. $ATH #ATH #AIInfrastructure #GPU @duostech #B300 #AI https://t.co/6cAglwEjkT","url":"https://x.com/TimeIsMoneyHQ/status/2113374711430238355"},{"author_id":"1973441574186131462","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:17:57.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113379353790681588"],"entities":{"urls":[{"description":"AWS has added Training Sessions to SageMaker, giving developers more control over model-training steps while AWS manages the GPU work. The service is aimed at teams building models that need to learn from sequences of actions, such as agents that use tools. Its distinction is not that SageMaker can now fine-tune models or run reinforcement learning; both were already available. It is that teams can shape more of the training loop without configuring the underlying GPU infrastructure.","display_url":"dataist.ai/news/aws-adds-…","end":227,"expanded_url":"https://dataist.ai/news/aws-adds-sagemaker-training-control-without-gpu-management/","images":[{"height":1024,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113379359130095616/FOmtBKLK?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1536},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2113379359130095616/FOmtBKLK?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":204,"status":200,"title":"AWS adds SageMaker training control without GPU management","unwound_url":"https://dataist.ai/news/aws-adds-sagemaker-training-control-without-gpu-management/","url":"https://t.co/sNEYzLEv0I"}]},"id":"2113379353790681588","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":0,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"AWS adds SageMaker training control without GPU management\n\nTraining Sessions lets SageMaker teams shape more of the training loop, but AWS offers no customer data on accuracy, cost or deployment speed.\n\nhttps://t.co/sNEYzLEv0I","url":"https://x.com/neuronium_ai/status/2113379353790681588"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2113385066978017281"]},"author_id":"767911033","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:42:15.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113385470101221670"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/KMuv6jJitu","end":302,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Andreyzila/status/2113385470101221670/photo/1","media_key":"3_2113385066978017281","start":279,"url":"https://t.co/KMuv6jJitu"}]},"id":"2113385470101221670","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":2,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"flapping airplanes raised $1b nine months after a $180m seed that valued it at $1.5b, reportedly $6b now. the  product is a megakernel: training, inference and vg in a single gpu kernel, overlapping memory bound inference with compute bound training so the chip rarely sits idle https://t.co/KMuv6jJitu","url":"https://x.com/Andreyzila/status/2113385470101221670"},{"author_id":"1346351802111803393","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:58:29.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113389554095038560"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":28,"id":"117233133","start":19,"username":"cHHillee"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"x.com/modal/status/2…","end":242,"expanded_url":"https://twitter.com/modal/status/2113383878215827664","start":219,"url":"https://t.co/tyGwnw9cVA"}]},"id":"2113389554095038560","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":3,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"I've been a fan of @cHHillee ever since \"Making Deep Learning Go Brrrr From First Principles\". If you had the tools to maximize GPU efficiency, could you own your post-training destiny? \n\nAlso hi this is my first tweet https://t.co/tyGwnw9cVA","url":"https://x.com/micahisyong/status/2113389554095038560"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2113382478618501120"]},"author_id":"1551987185372512263","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:35:55.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113383878215827664"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/I04rPmM2Yq","end":297,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/modal/status/2113383878215827664/video/1","media_key":"13_2113382478618501120","start":274,"url":"https://t.co/I04rPmM2Yq"}]},"id":"2113383878215827664","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":13,"impression_count":823,"like_count":39,"quote_count":2,"reply_count":3,"retweet_count":5},"text":"Tinker changed how people do post-training. We're big fans, and so are many of the teams we work with. But as those teams scale up, they keep raising the same two problems: per-token pricing gets expensive quickly, and you’re limited to the models and features the provider https://t.co/I04rPmM2Yq","url":"https://x.com/modal/status/2113383878215827664"},{"author_id":"1928480883717410816","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:03:27.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113375707321491485"],"id":"2113375707321491485","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":3,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"A 30k-step training run cost us $0.26 of GPU time. Compute was never the expensive part; the feedback loop was. So we shipped a snapshot gate: evals now deploy and invoke mid-run checkpoints instead of waiting for the finish line. Tighten the loop, compound the work.","url":"https://x.com/VargasJRDev/status/2113375707321491485"},{"author_id":"1551376741402349568","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:13:46.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113378301305893272"],"entities":{"cashtags":[{"end":233,"start":229,"tag":"ATH"}],"hashtags":[{"end":238,"start":234,"tag":"ATH"},{"end":249,"start":239,"tag":"Inference"},{"end":253,"start":250,"tag":"AI"}],"mentions":[{"end":30,"id":"1531588175000268800","start":18,"username":"AethirCloud"}],"urls":[{"description":"Discover how AI inference spending surpassed training workloads in 2026 and why Aethir’s distributed GPU infrastructure is a great fit for inference workloads.","display_url":"aethir.com/blog-posts/ai-…","end":278,"expanded_url":"https://aethir.com/blog-posts/ai-inference-spending-passed-training-the-55-shift","images":[{"height":900,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112668811631771649/wjUYYQ1e?format=jpg&name=orig","width":1600},{"height":150,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2112668811631771649/wjUYYQ1e?format=jpg&name=150x150","width":150}],"start":255,"status":200,"title":"AI Inference Spending Passed Training: The 55% Shift | Aethir","unwound_url":"https://aethir.com/blog-posts/ai-inference-spending-passed-training-the-55-shift","url":"https://t.co/vsjMSmzx0d"}]},"id":"2113378301305893272","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":28,"like_count":1,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"1/2🧵👇🏻\n🧠 Oct. 13: @AethirCloud says AI inference now accounts for 55% of AI-optimized IaaS spend in 2026—$23.3B vs $19B for training. Aethir argues distributed GPU supply fits inference better as demand shifts to serving models. $ATH #ATH #Inference #AI! https://t.co/vsjMSmzx0d","url":"https://x.com/TimeIsMoneyHQ/status/2113378301305893272"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2113382056222744578"]},"author_id":"416406628","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:28:43.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113382064741294301"],"entities":{"hashtags":[{"end":41,"start":30,"tag":"Neolclouds"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/3Wk4Ij5uvo","end":304,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/MarwaTechSpot/status/2113382064741294301/photo/1","media_key":"3_2113382056222744578","start":281,"url":"https://t.co/3Wk4Ij5uvo"}]},"id":"2113382064741294301","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":43,"like_count":3,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Why everyone is talking about #Neolclouds ?\n\nTraining AI models and running inference require:\n▫️ GPUs\n▫️ High-performance storage\n▫️ Seamless data access\n▫️ Mature security\n▫️ Integrated infrastructure \n\nThe right performance should be delivered at a sustainable cost.\n\nNeoclouds https://t.co/3Wk4Ij5uvo","url":"https://x.com/MarwaTechSpot/status/2113382064741294301"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2113379004103245824"]},"author_id":"1998705414322720768","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:16:56.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113379100081439129"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/R3ImglYubL","end":300,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/OmnimesOfficial/status/2113379100081439129/photo/1","media_key":"3_2113379004103245824","start":277,"url":"https://t.co/R3ImglYubL"}]},"id":"2113379100081439129","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":6,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"For $399 you get a robot that you can train a new gait for in one to two hours on a single GPU.\n\nMicroduck is a 25 cm biped from Pollen Robotics (the robotics team at Hugging Face), with 15 motors and a weight under 800 grams. At GTC Berlin on October 21, Jensen Huang brought https://t.co/R3ImglYubL","url":"https://x.com/OmnimesOfficial/status/2113379100081439129"},{"author_id":"1165159200470650881","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:52:52.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113388142787244520"],"id":"2113388142787244520","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":7,"like_count":0,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Modal released Spindle on October 22. It is an open-source training server that uses the same API as Thinking Machines' Tinker, and it runs inside your own Modal workspace.\n\nYou deploy it with one command. Billing follows GPU time instead of tokens. Modal says it built Spindle","url":"https://x.com/AIQuanting/status/2113388142787244520"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2113376548279525376","3_2113376548292075520","3_2113376548287836161","3_2113376548271030274"]},"author_id":"94877778","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:32.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2113377738690003006"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/WWdhHkZl4L","end":296,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/MisterSnowCrash/status/2113377738690003006/photo/1","media_key":"3_2113376548279525376","start":273,"url":"https://t.co/WWdhHkZl4L"},{"display_url":"pic.x.com/WWdhHkZl